  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Cottage pie is seasoned minced beef in a gravy, topped with mashed potato and baked in a dish until the top is golden. It serves four from a single pie dish and freezes very well. The key is "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "browning",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "browning"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " the mince properly before anything else goes in, which gives the filling its colour and depth."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Shepherd's pie uses lamb; cottage pie uses beef. The name comes from the farmers who kept cattle rather than sheep. Beyond that, the method is the same."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
